@peanut0brain No, the AI stocks that they were running up out of nowhere like MXL, FORM, SMTC, P, AMD, HPE, etc. The buying euphoria several weeks ago happened during major macro economic pressures including banks pulling back on data center funding which is why I deem it euphoria.

 I can see running these up post election but it seemed to happen during quarter end in September. Premature run up and now all of the sudden, just days later, we desperately need a major rotation, sell off, and repricing. Some big money managers are lunatics in a casino. It was just running the stocks up to dump them at the top after analysts were pulling new all time high targets out of their butts.(head fakes for Joe retail....$3000 Micron anyone?) Institutions make money when people buy the stocks that they give price targets for.

 Most of these ai stocks should have never reached anywhere near June 2026 highs.

